  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOL: Youth Catalysts: Strengthening Moldova&apos;s Democratic Core</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moldova&#x2019;s EU integration depends not only on institutional reforms but also on addressing the social drivers that weaken democratic resilience. This project will foster a more resilient and inclusive democracy at the community level, directly addressing youth disengagement and outmigration while embedding good-governance principles that reinforce trust in democratic institutions and advance Moldova&#x2019;s EU aspirations.
Among the most pressing concerns is youth outmigration: one in three young Moldovans intend to leave, citing disconnection, lack of voice, and limited opportunities for civic and economic participation. Political engagement remains fragile with youth turnout at only 26% in the 2023 local elections.  Exclusion is sharpest among NEET youth, rural girls, and young people with disabilities. Key drivers include limited local economic opportunities; weak civic/political education; low intergenerational dialogue and adult gatekeeping; inaccessible services and transport (especially for youth with disabilities); and perceptions that public institutions are unresponsive.
The project scales up proven, inclusive models of youth empowerment and civic participation to address these drivers directly.</narrative>
  </description>
